<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-1061] BookieWatcher should not do ZK blocking operations from ZK async callback thread</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-1061</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In some cases, the BookieWatcher can get the ZK event thread stuck. This happens when a ZK blocking request is issued from a ZK callback thread. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We should decouple the blocking requests in a separate executor to avoid deadlocking ZK client.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
